    "problem_statement": "Class decorator tearDown methods not properly restored after freezegun usage\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen using freezegun's class decorator on unittest test classes, the original `tearDown` and `tearDownClass` methods are not being properly restored after the decorator is applied. This causes issues when test classes have custom teardown logic that needs to be preserved.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport unittest\nimport datetime\nfrom freezegun import freeze_time\n\n@freeze_time(\"2013-04-09\")\nclass TestWithTearDown(unittest.TestCase):\n    @classmethod\n    def setUpClass(cls):\n        cls.setup_called = True\n    \n    @classmethod\n    def tearDownClass(cls):\n        cls.teardown_called = True\n    \n    def setUp(self):\n        self.instance_setup = True\n    \n    def tearDown(self):\n        self.instance_teardown = True\n    \n    def test_something(self):\n        self.assertEqual(datetime.date(2013, 4, 9), datetime.date.today())\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    unittest.main()\n```\n\nThe test class's `tearDown` and `tearDownClass` methods are not being called properly, which can lead to resource leaks or incomplete cleanup in test suites."
  }
